00:00:49.000 --> 00:01:42.000
But years of research have failed to find that abortion itself causes these outcomes. So how does obtaining an abortion or being denied one affect mental health and well-being? What are the effects of laws that limit access to abortion, such as those that mandate waiting periods or pre-abortion counseling? And how might new laws that outlaw abortion affect people, even in parts of the country, where abortion remains legal? Welcome to Speaking of Psychology, the flagship podcast of the American Psychological Association that examines the links between psychological science and everyday life. I'm Kim Mills. Our guest today is Dr. Antonia Biggs, a social psychologist and associate professor at the advancing new standards in reproductive health program at the University of California, San Francisco.
但多年的研究未能发现堕胎本身会导致这些后果。那么，进行堕胎或被拒绝堕胎如何影响心理健康和福祉？限制堕胎的法律（例如强制等待期或堕胎前咨询）有什么影响？即使在堕胎仍然合法的地区，新的堕胎禁令又会如何影响人们？欢迎收听美国心理学会的旗舰播客《心理学谈话》，该节目探讨心理科学与日常生活之间的联系。我是金·米尔斯。我们今天的嘉宾是安东尼娅·比格斯博士，她是社会心理学家，也是加州大学旧金山分校“推进生殖健康新标准”项目的副教授。

