health outcomes in the analyses of the turnaway data. But the study also looked at other outcomes like physical health and the economic effects of getting or being denied an abortion. What were some of the highlights of those findings? Yeah. So what we found, when we look at all the other outcomes that we looked at, we found that the people who were denying abortion were much more likely to experience economic hardship and economic insecurity that lasted for years. This impacted the financial well-being of the people who were denying abortion as well as their children and families, so they were much more likely to live in poverty. We also found that people who were experiencing intimate partner violence were significantly more likely to be tethered to those
