of people that we included in this study. And nobody who had an abortion. died. So we found, you know, very severe consequences to their physical health. What are the biggest challenges of doing this type of research? Was it hard to collect the sample? Was it difficult to structure the questions in a way that would get you what you needed? Tell us about that. Well, I think that one of the reasons why we haven't had good data up until the turnaway study is because of the challenges conducting this kind of research. So you can't randomize people to an abortion group or not abortion group ethically for obvious reasons. And so that has led to a lot of correlational studies that don't take into account some of, some important factors that could predispose people to negative mental health outcomes.
而堕胎的人中没有人死亡。所以我们发现，这对她们的身体健康造成了非常严重的后果。做这类研究最大的挑战是什么？收集样本难吗？以一种能得到所需结果的方式构建问题是否困难？请告诉我们。嗯，我认为直到“拒之门外研究”之前我们一直没有好的数据，原因之一就是进行此类研究的挑战。出于显而易见的原因，你不能在伦理上将人们随机分配到堕胎组或非堕胎组。因此，这导致了许多相关性研究，这些研究没有考虑到可能使人们容易产生负面心理健康结果的一些重要因素。

